{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Most Wondrous Itinerary for a Journey to the Land of Nippon**\n\n**Act I Scene I** – *The Departure*\nHark! Thou dost embark upon a voyage most grand toward the fair isle of Japan. Prepare thy spirit with noble attire and a heart full of wonder. From distant shores thou shalt sail upon the wings of steel until thou dost alight in the bustling realm of Tokyo.\n\n**Act I Scene II** – *The Imperial City of Tokyo*\nSeven days thou shalt tarry in this metropolis where ancient and modern dance as twain.\nFirst morn: Seek the sacred grounds of the Meiji Shrine where cedars whisper prayers to the gods.\nSecond day: Wander the stalls of Asakusa’s market where treasures of paper and porcelain do gleam.\nThird eve: Ascend the towering spire of Tokyo Skytree and behold the city’s heart laid bare beneath thee.\nFourth morn: Journey to the hallowed halls of the Imperial Palace and marvel at the seat of emperors past.\nFifth day: Delve into the electric dreams of Akihabara where gadgets and fantasies entwine.\nSixth eve: Savor the delights of Tsukiji’s outer market where fish of every hue and fin do tempt thy palate.\nSeventh day: Rest thy feet in Ueno Park where cherry blossoms in season paint the earth in hues of pink.\n\n**Act II Scene I** – *The Ancient Capital of Kyoto*\nHie thee hence upon the swift rails of the Shinkansen to Kyoto where the ghosts of samurai and geisha do linger.\nFirst morn: Bow before the golden visage of Kinkaku-ji the Temple of the Golden Pavilion.\nSecond day: Pray in the hallowed halls of Kiyomizu-dera where the earth itself is sacred.\nThird eve: Wander the philosopher’s path along the canal where maples blush in autumn’s embrace.\nFourth morn: Lose thyself in the bamboo groves of Arashiyama where shafts of light dance like spirits.\nFifth day: Attend a tea ceremony most refined and learn the art of serenity.\nSixth eve: Feast upon kaiseki’s bounty under lanterns of paper and flame.\n\n**Act III Scene I** – *The Sacred Isle of Miyajima*\nTake ship to the isle of Miyajima where torii gates float upon the tide.\nFirst morn: Stand before the great vermilion gate of Itsukushima Shrine and watch as the sea doth claim it.\nSecond day: Ascend Mount Misen and behold the sea of Japan spread below like a tapestry woven of sapphire and silver.\n\n**Act IV Scene I** – *The Culinary Triumphs of Osaka*\nJourney to Osaka the kitchen of the realm.\nFirst morn: Gorge upon takoyaki and okonomiyaki where flavors do battle upon thy tongue.\nSecond eve: Laugh and cheer in Dotonbori where neon signs do shout in tongues unknown.\n\n**Act V Scene I** – *The Serpentine Path of Nara*\nTurn thy steps to Nara where deer do bow and temples do dream.\nFirst morn: Visit Todai-ji and gaze upon the Buddha’s countenance so vast it toucheth the heavens.\nSecond day: Feed the sacred deer who wander free and bow before thy presence.\n\n**Act VI Scene I** – *The Farewell*\nReturn to Tokyo with a heart full of memories and a trunk heavy with treasures.\nFinal morn: Last-minute purchases in Shinjuku’s malls where trinkets of every sort do call thy name.\nFinal eve: Raise a cup of sake to thine adventures and bid adieu to the land of the rising sun.\n\nThus doth thy journey end but never thy tale for Japan’s wonders shall echo in thy soul forevermore.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -1.3030120134353638}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.07401636242866516}, {"token": " Most", "logprob": -0.2740887701511383}, {"token": " W", "logprob": -0.3884752690792084}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -1.1444026313256472e-05}, {"token": "rous", "logprob": -2.622600959512056e-06}, {"token": " It", "logprob": -0.28655242919921875}, {"token": "iner", "logprob": -0.0002548369811847806}, {"token": "ary", "logprob": -0.0033669944386929274}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.03495996817946434}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.21049784123897552}, {